Title: Backend — Python ProjectRole

Stack & Versions
- Python 3.12 (prefer 3.11+ features: typing, asyncio)
- Web: FastAPI + Uvicorn (gunicorn for prod)
- Data: MongoDB (motor), Redis (redis-py), Kafka (confluent-kafka or aiokafka)
- Search: Elasticsearch (elastic-transport/elasticsearch)
- Validation & Settings: pydantic v2 + pydantic-settings
- Testing: pytest + pytest-asyncio + httpx (AsyncClient) + pytest-cov
- Lint/Format: ruff (lint/isort) + black
- Types: mypy (strict-ish), typing-extensions if needed
- Observability: prometheus-client, OpenTelemetry (optional), standard logging (JSON)
- Packaging: uv/poetry/pip-tools (choose one; default to uv or poetry)
- Runtime: Docker; deploy to Kubernetes (12-factor)

Project Structure
- src/
  app/                     # FastAPI app factory, routers, dependencies
  app/api/                 # routers: v1/*.py (auth, items, health)
  app/core/                # config, logging, security, constants
  app/services/            # business logic (pure/async services)
  app/db/                  # mongo motor client, redis, kafka producers/consumers
  app/models/              # pydantic models & schemas
  app/repositories/        # data-access layer (Mongo/ES/Kafka I/O)
  app/workers/             # background jobs (Celery/RQ/custom consumers)
  app/integrations/        # external APIs/adapters
  app/metrics/             # prometheus metrics, middleware
  app/utils/               # helpers (retry, time, id, serialization)
  tests/                   # unit/integration/e2e (mirror src layout)
- pyproject.toml           # black/ruff/mypy/pytest config
- .env, .env.example       # environment samples (do not commit secrets)
- docker/                  # Dockerfile(s), compose overrides
- k8s/                     # manifests/helm values (if applicable)
- Makefile                 # dev shortcuts
- README.md                # how to run/test/deploy

Conventions
- Comments, docstrings, commit messages in English.
- Async-first: use async def for I/O (motor, aiokafka, redis.async)
- Dependency injection via FastAPI Depends; thin endpoints, fat services.
- Pydantic models for request/response; never expose internal DB shapes directly.
- Separate schemas: In/Out/Internal. Validate external input with zod-like rigor (pydantic).
- Configuration only via env (pydantic-settings). No hardcoded creds/URLs.
- Return structured errors (problem+json style where relevant).
- Logging: JSON to stdout; include trace_id/request_id, user_id when available.
- Metrics: expose /metrics with Prometheus; instrument HTTP latency, Kafka lag, DB ops.
- Time in UTC; store ISO 8601; avoid naive datetimes.

Quality Gates
- CI runs: ruff + black --check + mypy + pytest -q
- Coverage target ≥ 80% for core services and critical paths.
- No failing mypy (strict = True for app/*).
- Pre-commit hooks for ruff/black.

Security
- Validate all inputs; size limits for payloads; file uploads behind checks.
- Use proper CORS; secure cookies (HttpOnly, SameSite), auth via JWT/OIDC where needed.
- Secrets from env or secret manager; never commit secrets.
- Sanitize logs; no PII unless required and masked.

API Style
- Versioned routes: /api/v1/*
- Use app factory pattern: create_app(config) to ease testing.
- Add /healthz (liveness) and /readyz (readiness) endpoints.
- OpenAPI enabled; include tags, examples, response models & error models.

Datastores & Messaging
- Mongo (motor): central client with lifecycle hooks (startup/shutdown).
- Repositories return domain models; no framework objects leaking upward.
- Redis: for caching, rate limits, short-lived state; define TTLs explicitly.
- Kafka: define topic names, key/value schemas; consumers idempotent; DLQ strategy documented.

Observability
- Structured logging: {"level","ts","msg","logger","trace_id","span_id","path","status"}
- Prometheus middlewares for HTTP; counters/gauges/histograms for DB/Kafka.
- Optional: OpenTelemetry for traces (FastAPI, motor, aiokafka instrumentations).

Testing Strategy
- Unit tests for services/utils (pure logic)
- Integration tests with ephemeral Mongo/Redis/ES via docker-compose or testcontainers
- API tests with httpx.AsyncClient (startup/shutdown lifespan)
- Fixtures for app(), test clients, fake repos, factories for schemas
- Contract tests for Kafka producers/consumers when feasible

Makefile Targets (baseline)
- make install        # install deps (uv/poetry/pip-tools)
- make fmt            # black .
- make lint           # ruff check .
- make fix            # ruff --fix && black .
- make type           # mypy src
- make test           # pytest -q
- make cov            # pytest --cov=src --cov-report=term-missing
- make run            # uvicorn app.main:app --reload
- make up/down/logs   # docker compose dev stack

Deliverables When Generating Code
- Provide full file paths and contents (ready to paste).
- Include any new dependencies + exact install commands.
- Add/modify tests to keep coverage and examples runnable.
- Update README with quickstart if the change impacts local run.

Common Scaffolds (what to generate by default)
1) FastAPI app factory with settings, logging, /healthz, /readyz, /metrics
2) Mongo motor client module with graceful startup/shutdown
3) Example router (GET/POST) with pydantic In/Out models and validation
4) Service + repository pattern example (async)
5) Kafka producer/consumer skeleton (idempotent, graceful stop, metrics)
6) Prometheus middleware + custom metrics example
7) Pytest fixtures: app(), client(), mongo(), redis(), kafka()
8) Dockerfile (slim, multi-stage) + docker-compose for dev (Mongo, Redis, Kafka, ES, Prometheus, Grafana)
9) pyproject.toml preconfigured for black/ruff/mypy/pytest
10) pre-commit config with black/ruff hooks

Performance
- Avoid N+1 in repos; create indices; use bounded concurrency (asyncio.Semaphore).
- Reuse clients (mongo/redis/kafka) instead of reconnecting per request.
- Cache hot reads in Redis with explicit invalidation.

Docs
- Keep README concise: setup, run, test, lint, type-check.
- Document environment variables in .env.example with safe defaults.

Windows Notes
- Use cross-platform commands in Makefile (or provide .ps1 equivalents).
- Prefer uv or poetry for reliable, reproducible installs on Windows.

Optional Integrations
- Datadog exporter for traces/metrics/logs (opt-in).
- OpenAPI clients generated for consumers if needed.
